    {
      "name": "Introduction",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 76,
          "w": 258,
          "h": 130,
          "text": "Haldane was a small watchmaker in the Lower Levels that assembled mechanical wristwatches entirely by hand. It closed after its third and last production run, and no one on the Station has the tools or the patience to build one today.\n\nThis guide will provide everything you need to know to appraise the value of any Haldane watch.",
          "translations": {
            "ja": "ハルデーンは、下層世界にあった小さな時計工房で、機械式腕時計をすべて手作業で組み立てていました。第3生産ロットを最後に閉業し、今のステーションには、同じものを作る道具も根気もある者はいません。\n\n本ガイドでは、あらゆるハルデーンの時計の価格を判断するために必要な情報を掲載いたします。",
            "zh": "霍尔丹是下层区一家小型钟表工坊，所有机械腕表都由手工组装。它在第三批也是最后一批生产后关门，如今空间站里没人有工具或耐心去造一块。\n\n本指南将提供鉴定任何霍尔丹手表价值所需的全部信息。"
          },
          "style": "body",
          "align": "left",
          "valign": "top",
          "fontSize": 6,
          "color": "#373541"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 212,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 56,
          "text": "Regardless of condition, a Haldane watch has a base value of 360 Credits, and a minimum value of 120 Credits.",
          "translations": {
            "ja": "状態に関わらず、ハルデーンの時計の基本価格は360クレジットで、最低価格は120クレジットです。",
            "zh": "无论品相如何，霍尔丹手表的基础价值均为360信用点，且最低价值为120信用点。"
          },
          "style": "body",
          "align": "left",
          "valign": "top",
          "fontSize": 6,
          "color": "#373541"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "x": 206,
          "y": 208,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 160,
          "sprite": "wg_full",
          "fit": "stretch"
        }
      ],
      "template": "guide_page",
      "slots": {
        "header": "Station Trade Commission",
        "title": "Haldane Watch Appraisal Guide",
        "body": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Run and Metal",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 74,
          "w": 258,
          "h": 14,
          "text": "1. Run and Metal",
          "translations": {
            "ja": "1. ロットと金属",
            "zh": "1. 批次与金属"
          },
          "style": "label",
          "align": "left",
          "valign": "middle",
          "fontSize": 7.5,
          "color": "#355271"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 90,
          "w": 258,
          "h": 20,
          "text": "The dial color tells which production run a watch came from. The case metal is read from the bezel and the lugs.",
          "translations": {
            "ja": "文字盤の色で、どの生産ロットの時計かが分かります。ケースの金属は、ベゼルとラグ（ベルトの付け根）で見分けます。",
            "zh": "表盘颜色表明这块表出自哪一批生产。表壳的金属从表圈和表耳上辨认。"
          },
          "style": "body",
          "align": "left",
          "valign": "top",
          "fontSize": 5.5,
          "color": "#373541"
        },
